mps.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-oj[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-oj/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Group-link grammar, one resolver, and the [N / ]N commands[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-grammar[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-grammar: in bob-navigation-hotkeys, tighten the `\\[n`/`]n` matcher so[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]doubled arrows never step, recognize `«`/`»` (typed `<<`/`>>`) group [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]links on link-only nav lines, build the one resolver (authored, then the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Ledger Tools provider), add the group commands with the creation guard [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and repeat guard, route `[{`/`]}` on family `n`, publish [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`walkMode.links` v7, and map `[N`/`]N` in the vault vimrc.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Calendar group provider, legacy step fill-in, and the [/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]pre-adoption guard[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]calendar-groups[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]calendar-groups: in bob-ledger-tools, add the `api.navGroups` v1 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]provider for daily, week, and quarter group stops plus derived step [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stops for notes without a written nav link, classify every target as [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing, creatable, or ghost, and make `periodNotes.ensureNote` refuse [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pre-adoption past years.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Album `walk_by` and group-major record walk lines in bob[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]walk-by-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]walk-by-cli: in bob-cli, add the album `walk_by` key (non-list choices [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]field), order `ring_slots` group-major, rewrite at most five walk lines [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]when a record's `walk_by` value changes, report groups and group heads [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in albums and records JSON with a `record_walk_groups_v1` capability, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add the `bob albums update` set/unset op, strip `«`/`»` from walk [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]labels, extend the shared golden vectors, and document it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Grouped record walk model and the record group provider[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]record-groups[dim] · [dim][/dim]after walk-by-cli, calendar-groups[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]record-groups: in bob-ledger-tools, mirror bob's group-major order in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the record walk model from the shared vectors, gate sync requests on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob's capability, and extend `api.navGroups` with record group stops [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](heads of the neighboring occupied groups, wrapping).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The group row at the bottom of property cards[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]group-rail[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-grammar, calendar-groups, record-groups[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]group-rail: add the kit group-row builder and the shared missing-target [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]look (dashed `+` creatable, dotted ghost), adopt it on day, week, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]quarter cards and the record walk rail, give legacy dailies a derived [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]step row, add the album card's \"walks by\" pill, and prove the look in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the preview matrix.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Group arms and hints in the links walker footer[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]links-footer[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-grammar, calendar-groups, record-groups[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]links-footer: add outer `«`/`»` group arms, the current-group context, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the `]} next week` and boundary hints, ghost and creatable arm states, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]end-first shedding, and re-validated arm activation through the group [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commands.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Album adoption, real-Obsidian proof, and final deploy[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]adopt-and-prove[dim] · [dim][/dim]after group-rail, links-footer[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]adopt-and-prove: verify every host runs plugins and a bob that support [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]grouped walks, set `walk_by` on the zettel, subscriptions, and eat [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]albums (plus movies and podcasts if accepted), sync them, add a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]real-Obsidian group-jump e2e, run the existing walk, footer, card, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]title-block e2e suites, and deploy the final tree.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Accepted memory updates[/bold #D7AFFF]                                       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]glossary[dim] · [dim][/dim]after adopt-and-prove[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]glossary: apply only the memory decisions answered yes, then run `sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory init`.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-oj","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-oj.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"s